From 039edfed6e0037835cf34e30df41e22732644a05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caleb Jones <caleb@calebgj.io>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:20:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] arch, vmm: riscv64: Describe the vCPU topology in the FDT

--cpus topology=... was ignored on riscv64: the FDT only listed the
harts, so the guest saw every vCPU as its own core with no cluster or
socket grouping.

Emit a cpu-map node (socket/cluster/core/thread) the same way aarch64
does. Dies are described as clusters, so a guest can mirror hosts that
group cores in several clusters per socket, e.g. topology=1:4:2:1 for
two clusters of four cores. The map is only emitted when the topology
covers exactly the booted harts, since there is no CPU hotplug on
riscv64 and the map must not reference missing CPU nodes.

Also add FDT unit tests for the cpu-map and the ISA properties.

Signed-off-by: Caleb Jones <caleb@calebgj.io>
---
 arch/src/riscv64/fdt.rs | 145 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 arch/src/riscv64/mod.rs |   2 +
 vmm/src/vm.rs           |   3 +
 3 files changed, 149 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

